  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This outcome supports Jordan&#x2019;s efforts to strengthen the ratification, implementation and reporting of international labour standards through enhanced capacity of the Government, employers&#x2019; organizations and workers&#x2019; organizations. It addresses labour governance, compliance with international obligations, and the effective realization of fundamental principles and rights at work.

During the biennium, the ILO will support tripartite constituents to improve labour legislation, policies and practices in line with international labour standards, strengthen mechanisms for social dialogue and labour standards reporting. Support will also be provided to advance the application of sector-specific labour standards in priority sectors.

Expected results include stronger national capacity to implement and monitor international labour standards, improved tripartite engagement in labour governance, and enhanced protection of workers&#x2019; rights. Beneficiaries include government institutions, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, labour inspectors, and workers and employers across Jordan, particularly women, youth, persons with disabilities and workers in vulnerable situations. Implementation will be undertaken in partnership with national stakeholders, the United Nations system and development partners.</narrative>
  </description>
